**Proposition 12.2 (unnormalized effects and actual laws).** In each saturated attaining instrument the explicit high encoder per report is

$$
\sqrt{(1+rs\tau)/2}\,K(v)E^\dagger:\mathbb C^5\to\mathbb C^3,
$$

with decoder $X\mapsto EXE^\dagger$. For every rank-many low factor $z_{rj}$ of $L_r$, its encoder is $U_{rj}^\dagger K(z_{rj})E^\dagger$ into $\mathbb C^2$, with decoder $X\mapsto EU_{rj}XU_{rj}^\dagger E^\dagger$. Supported failure rows and complement trace branches are exactly those in Theorem 3.4, retaining their separate report/eigenpair labels and entire scalar measures. The same construction with high factors $\sqrt{k/2}e_D$ gives the plane instruments.

For a positive five-mode test $\sigma$ with unnormalized compression $\rho$, their raw branch masses are the traces of these encoder outputs; in particular

$$
\begin{aligned}
p(r,H)&=\frac{1+rs\tau}{2}\operatorname{tr}(\Theta(P)\rho),\\
