\tag{PG.65}
$$

Only on a normalized actual input are these probabilities. On each original history the last line is
$1/2+rs\kappa en\sqrt{y(64-y)}/128$. A fair report at $s=0$ does not make the finer generated labels input independent.

Proof. These are encoder Born traces. The low reconstruction isometry preserves its trace, and the sum is precisely the effect (PG.10), whose trace gives the last line. No trace is divided by a later-live, failure or acquisition mass. Whole TP decoding, full reference operators, every separate Borel time set, cross-support zeros and extra-sector zeros have already been proved at the map level in Theorem 3.4 and therefore hold for all these specializations. $\square$

